# Findings the secret scan is right to flag by shape and wrong to flag in fact.
#
# Each line is a fingerprint: <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>. Add one only when
# the finding is demonstrably not a secret, and say why — an ignore file nobody
# can audit is worse than a scan nobody runs.

# A verification step in a plan document:
#   curl ... -H "Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token"
# The rule fires on the SHAPE `Authorization: Bearer <value>`, whatever the
# value is; here the value is the words "not-a-real-token", used to prove the
# endpoint answers 401. The doc has since been rewritten to pass the value
# through a shell variable (which is why the real `Bearer ${ADMIN_TOKEN}` in
# cloud-sweep.yml never tripped this), but the string stays in this commit's
# history and the scan reads history.
